{"kind":"assert","text":"The public live-runtime candidate at a3b9e069, artifact d6464e33, has a sound externally signed frame protocol but is not safe for public browser use yet. OpenSession publishes presence and consumes the per-key session quota before proof of private-key possession, so an attacker can impersonate a victim watcher and occupy all slots. Public OpenSession and RenewSession accept unbounded actor/value strings and arbitrarily long positive TTLs, weakening memory and lease bounds. The runtime also exposes only its live cursor; chess item 5 needs an application-neutral way to join durable frontier notifications with live changes while keeping the cursors distinct. Repair the current-main recut before review: add bounded expiring single-use proof-of-key session opening (or an equally fail-closed pending lease), enforce exported actor/value/TTL limits at open and renew, and expose a composition seam for durable frontier notification without importing Workroom semantics into host/live. Preserve deterministic browser signing bytes and keep durable intent encoding out of this package.","body":{"candidate":"1e48ef972338da8037d878657d4f2f7f34446cbc","severity":"blocking","status":"open"}}